checklist.batch_gate:
Convention check (NOT runtime-enforced). ① Quick grep (flawed, assistive only): first ENUMERATE the full call-site set with grep -rnE "_client\.chat\(|chat_stream\(" backend/scripts evals, then judge each line — do NOT grep for 'no_cache' to 'find guard evidence' (that is selection bias and hides omissions). Limitations: (a) false-positive — it flags capture_eval.py:183 METHOD DEFINITION 'def chat_stream(self, ..., no_cache: bool, ...)' as a call site => must exclude 'def ' lines; (b) false-negative — single-line grep cannot see multi-line calls '_client.chat(\n token,\n q,\n)'. ② AST version (recommended, fixes false-negative): walk ast.Call, check func tail-name in {chat, chat_stream} and keywords has no_cache=True; shape follows repo precedent observability._ACCOUNT_FIELDS. Write as a .py file and run (avoid -c inline expansion pitfalls):
  import ast, pathlib
  ROOT = pathlib.Path("backend/scripts")
  for p in ROOT.rglob("*.py"):
      try: tree = ast.parse(p.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
      except SyntaxError: continue
      for n in ast.walk(tree):
          if isinstance(n, ast.Call):
              name = getattr(n.func, "attr", getattr(n.func, "id", ""))
              if name in ("chat", "chat_stream"):
                  has = any(kw.arg == "no_cache" and isinstance(kw.value, ast.Constant) and kw.value.value is True for kw in n.keywords)
                  if not has:
                      print(f"LEAK {p.relative_to(ROOT)}:{n.lineno} {name}")
  => printed lines are the omitted call sites; reject pre-batch. ③ KNOWN DEFECT (bare-name false-positive): the func tail-name match also reports call sites of a LOCAL same-name 'def chat(...)' wrapper in the same file, even when that wrapper body already passes no_cache=True (e.g. acceptance.py:19, smoke_b1b5.py:15) — those do NOT actually leak. Two handling options: (a) manual dereference — after the gate prints a LEAK line, open that file and confirm whether it is a bare _client.chat( omission or a local wrapper that already passes True (the three-class split in prevented_detail is the worked example); (b) advanced (suggested shape, NOT implemented this round) — follow ast to the same-file FunctionDef of that name, recursively check whether its body contains the no_cache literal (one level of indirection dissolves the wrapper false-positive). Registry E2 stays BLOCKED precisely because this cannot be enforced at the request layer.
